@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 45 — "זיכוי בעד נטולי יכולת", the credit for a paralysed or blind child or a child with an intellectual-developmental
-- disability. Row IL-27. Source lines 1707-1712.
--
-- A resident individual who had in the tax year, or whose spouse had, a paralysed child, a blind child, or a child with an intellectual-developmental
-- disability, has two credit points for each such child, in his tax computation or his spouse's (a). The points are for a child for whom he
-- received no tax credit under s 44 (c). (b) is repealed. The Minister may set conditions (d): the regulations of 5756-1996 are not in
-- the source bundle; as in s 44 the caller states whether their conditions are met and the rule declines where not known and a point is at stake.
-- THE POINTS ARE IN HIS COMPUTATION OR HIS SPOUSE'S: how they are divided the text does not say. The record says whose computation takes them
-- (the individual's, the spouse's, or not stated); where not stated, an individual who has a spouse is declined (NOTES.md, fork F15).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 45 — a disabled child`

-- src:1708 | (א) יחיד תושב ישראל שהיה לו בשנת המס ילד משותק, ילד עיוור או ילד עם מוגבלות שכלית–התפתחותית או שהיה לבן זוגו ילד כאמור, יובאו בחשבון בחישוב המס שלו או של בן זוגו שתי נקודות זיכוי בשל כל ילד כאמור.
-- src:1709 | (ב) [note: (בוטל).]
-- src:1710 | (ג) יחיד יהיה זכאי לנקודות הזיכוי על פי סעיף קטן (א) רק אם לא קיבל זיכוי ממס עבור אותו ילד על פי סעיף 44.
-- src:1711 | (ד) שר האוצר רשאי לקבוע תנאים לזכאות לנקודות זיכוי על פי סעיף זה.
-- src:1712 | [note: פורסמו תקנות מס הכנסה (זיכוי בעד נטול יכולת וזיכוי בעד הוצאות בשל החזקת קרוב במוסד), התשנ״ו–1996; תקרת ההכנסה המזכה: בשנת 2023, 182,000 ש״ח ליחיד, 291,000 ש״ח לזוג; בשנים 2024–2027, 188,000 ש״ח ליחיד, 301,000 ש״ח לזוג.]

@ref ITO s 45(d), lines 1711-1712 — the regulations of 5756-1996 are not in the source bundle (needs a source)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 45 lets the Minister set conditions, the regulations of 5756-1996 are not in the source bundle, and here they may decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 45 lets the Minister set conditions, the regulations of 5756-1996 are not in the source bundle, and here they may decide"

@ref ITO s 45(a), line 1708; fork F15
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 45 gives the points in the computation of the individual or of his spouse and does not say how they are divided, and here he has a spouse` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 45 gives the points in the computation of the individual or of his spouse and does not say how they are divided, and here he has a spouse"

-- (a), (c): two points for each child who is paralysed, blind or has an intellectual-developmental disability, for whom no tax credit was
-- received under s 44.
@ref ITO s 45(a), (c), lines 1708, 1710
GIVEN c IS A `A child, for section 45`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45 — the points for` c MEANS
    IF   (c's `paralyzed` OR c's `blind` OR c's `has an intellectual-developmental disability`)
         AND NOT c's `a tax credit was received for the child under section 44`
    THEN 2
    ELSE 0

@ref ITO s 45(a), (c), (d), lines 1708-1711; fork F15
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual with children, for section 45`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45 — the points the children give, before the conditions of the regulations and the sharing between spouses, for` i MEANS
    IF   i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    THEN sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 45 — the points for` c) (i's `the individual's or the spouse's children in the tax year`))
    ELSE 0

@export The credit points under Income Tax Ordinance s 45 (a paralysed or blind child, or one with an intellectual-developmental disability) for a tax year from 2024: two points for each such child for whom no credit was received under s 44, in the computation the record names; declines where the regulations of 5756-1996 may decide, where an individual with a spouse does not say whose computation takes the points, and for a foreign worker (s 48A)
@ref ITO s 45, lines 1707-1712
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual with children, for section 45`
          @desc the tax year, residence, the children (paralysed, blind, disabled, credit received under s 44), whether he has a spouse, whose computation takes the points, and whether the conditions of the regulations are met
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 45 for` i MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-27 answers`
        (`the points, unless section 48A may take them from a foreign worker:` (i's `a foreign worker`) `,` `the points`)
    WHERE
        `before` MEANS `s 45 — the points the children give, before the conditions of the regulations and the sharing between spouses, for` i
        `after the conditions` MEANS
            CONSIDER i's `the conditions of the regulations made under section 45(d)`
            WHEN `met`       THEN `before`
            WHEN `not met`   THEN 0
            WHEN `not known` THEN IF `before` EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `section 45 lets the Minister set conditions, the regulations of 5756-1996 are not in the source bundle, and here they may decide`
        `the points` MEANS
            CONSIDER i's `whose computation takes the points`
            WHEN `the individual's` THEN `after the conditions`
            WHEN `the spouse's`     THEN 0
            WHEN `not stated`       THEN
                IF   i's `has a spouse` AND `after the conditions` GREATER THAN 0
                THEN `section 45 gives the points in the computation of the individual or of his spouse and does not say how they are divided, and here he has a spouse`
                ELSE `after the conditions`
